Subject: [PATCH] feat: bird house trapping on Fossil Island
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Bird house trapping on Fossil Island was not implemented.

Change. The four bird house spaces (multilocs on varps 1626-1629, the
values RuneLite's Time Tracking reads): build (or use a bird house on the
space) and add seeds: 10 low-level seeds, or 5 wildblood hop or
ranarr-and-higher herb seeds (mixing allowed). After 50 minutes Empty or
Reset gives the clockwork, 10 raw bird meat (always dropped to the
ground), 30-60 feathers, nests and the Hunter XP, with the collect
message RuneLite's Loot Tracker parses. The seed nest chance is the
skilling formula over the wiki chart (1/256 at level 1, 101/256 at 50,
201/256 at 99), then five rolls on the nest table. Emptying a house
early asks first, then keeps the clockwork and loses the house, seeds
and loot. Reset places a new house one tick later: a carried bird house
first, otherwise one built from logs and the clockwork with a hammer and
chisel (the bird house's Crafting level and XP). Tier data in the
server-only dbtable birdhouse_types (56003, rows 60163-60171; logs and
Crafting level/XP columns for Reset), server varps 63762-63769,
::birdhouses makes seeded houses full, own BirdHousePluginPack. Needs
the Hunter module skeleton PR.

Tests. Integration suite BirdHouseScriptTest (11): the Loot Tracker
pattern, the multiloc varps, tier order, nest and seed-nest chances
against the wiki charts, build/seed/wait/empty with the raw bird meat on
the ground, five high-level seeds and mixed seeds, emptying early, Reset
building an oak house from logs at Crafting 20, a full inventory.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Bird house trapping (levels, XP, seeds, nest
charts, early emptying, Reset), Bird house trapping/Seeds, Birdhouse
(scenery) (raw bird meat note, seed nest chart), the nine bird house
item pages (Crafting level, XP, logs). Varps from the cache; RuneLite
Time Tracking and Loot Tracker (BSD) for the values and the message.

Caveats. Guesses: the early-empty warning's wording, the other game
messages, the op layout per state. With several log types Reset builds
the best house the player can place instead of asking for the log type.
Not done: clue nests, the strung rabbit foot, crafting bird houses from
the inventory, building from materials on an empty space.

